        "math_academy_id": "q-342020",
        "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{4}{x}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{{e}^{3}}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
        "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{{e}^{3}}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{4}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-x){|}_{-1}^{1}\\,+\\,(4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}-1-(\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}-(-1))]\\,+\\,[4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({e}^{3})-4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}-1-(-\\frac{1}{3}+1)]\\,+\\,12 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
